00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.970 align:start position:0%
the council has discussed these two  files already over a year and I am happy  to say that we reached agreement both  with strong support from the Member  States  two years ago in Paris the EU promised  to cut emissions by at least 40 percent  by 2030 so we keep our promises the  lower CF regulation will make sure that  all emissions generated by use of soils  trees plants biomass and timber are  taken into account in the u.s. overall  target it will establish new accounting  rules and binding commitments for member  states to ensure that this sector will  always absorb at least as much co2 as it  emits the council also agreed on EU  priorities for the third United Nations  Environment Assembly meeting taking  place in December for sharing proposal  will reduce greenhouse gas emissions in  all sectors outside the repair Union  emissions training system such as  building transport waste and agriculture  up to 2030 through binding annual  targets for all member states the main  point of discussion has been the  presidency proposal for a safety reserve  allowing low-income member states some  more flexibility should they face  problems reaching their targets I remind  you that this is the first time in  European Union law that all member  states will have reduction targets with  the repeal Parliament having adopted  this negotiation position early this  year the adoption of the council  position is a major step forward to our  standing the proposals into clear  binding rules and preparations for trial  negotiations on both files can now begin
 

